  "overall_finding": "The selected q001 development input saving did not repeat in either confirmation pair. In the frozen new-task expansion, q002 scores 10/10 and passes in both arms with zg input +82.79% and wall +36.15%; q003 scores baseline 6/10 versus zg 9/10 but both fail core source evidence gates, with zg input +36.28% and wall +46.35%. No stable efficiency or passing-quality benefit is established; all results are retained. Remote Qwen embedding is operationally feasible, but its q001 pair trades a passing core citation gate (zg only) against factual points 9→8, input +25.74% and wall +48.65%; its joint signal rule fails. Architecture q004 scores baseline 7/10 versus zg 9/10, but both fail the frozen source-grounded endpoint. zg input increases 29.91%, agent wall falls 30.32%, and its measured setup plus agent time exceeds baseline agent time. This is a factual-score/latency/input tradeoff, not passing-quality or efficiency success. Shared-answer-verification q004 scores baseline 9/10 versus zg 9/10; source-grounded success is False versus False. Frozen candidate-quality signal=False, efficiency signal=False, stop-this-instruction-branch=True. This single post-observation development pair does not establish a stable favorable set or isolate the prompt's causal effect.",
  "interpretation_notes": [
    "efficiency_comparable is a per-trial completeness gate, not a claim of equal answer quality or retrieval benefit.",
    "Compare quality before resources; never pool protocols.",
    "V1 reflex zg had zero successful retrievals; token reduction is not retrieval benefit.",
    "zvec treatment raw partial usage is retained but excluded from token comparisons.",
    "Single pair per task per protocol; no statistical or contamination-free claim.",
    "Completion-v2 both arms stopped without a budget denial; do not attribute completion causally to forced denial.",
    "Completion-v2 score 9/10 does not mean every claim is correct: zg misses C4, baseline misses C7, and both have ancillary source errors. See full blinded review.",
    "Selected development pair is reported separately from future confirmation pairs; two replications of a selected task do not establish generalization.",
    "A factual score of 9/10 can still fail the source citation gate (r03 baseline); factual score, core citations and tool success must be reported separately.",
    "The frozen two-task expansion failed its set signal rule: q002 both answers pass, q003 neither passes despite zg scoring 9/10, and zg uses more input on both. Successful correct-root retrieval alone does not imply quality or efficiency benefit.",
    "Remote q001 improves the binary core source gate but lowers factual points and increases resources. Report these axes separately; do not call it general quality dominance or pool it with historical local embedding pairs.",
    "q004 both fail source-grounded success despite factual score 7→9 and lower zg agent wall. More input and 201.74 s of separate setup prohibit an efficiency or cold-start speedup claim. Old rules and all previous rows remain unchanged.",
    "Shared-answer-verification q004 scores baseline 9/10 versus zg 9/10; source-grounded success is False versus False. Frozen candidate-quality signal=False, efficiency signal=False, stop-this-instruction-branch=True. This single post-observation development pair does not establish a stable favorable set or isolate the prompt's causal effect."
  ],
